# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# Never commit .env.local — it is already git-ignored.

# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# NOTE: no trailing path (not /rest/v1/, /auth/v1/, etc.) — the Supabase
# client libraries append the correct path themselves.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase "publishable" API key (the current Supabase key format, sb_publishable_...).
# Safe to expose to the browser — Row Level Security, not key secrecy, protects data.
# See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7 for the full secrets/environment-variable policy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Supabase "secret" service-role key (sb_secret_... or a legacy service_role JWT).
# Bypasses Row Level Security. Server-only — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Not required for this milestone (auth foundation only); add when a server-only
# trusted operation actually needs it.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Shared secret for the daily company-greetings cron job (app/api/cron/greetings/route.ts).
# Generate any long random string. On Vercel, set this in the project's
# environment variables — Vercel Cron automatically sends it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` on its scheduled requests (see vercel.json).
# On any OTHER host, configure your own scheduler to send that same header
# daily; the route rejects every request without it.
# CRON_SECRET=
